# Purpose
This document describes only La Caracola backend-specific behavior.
Generic engineering rules: [Tech Doc](./tech-doc.mdc).
Product behavior: [Business Doc](./business-doc.mdc).
Data model: [Specific Data Model](./specific-data-model.md).

# Actual architecture
- Monolite Laravel MVC con Blade server-rendered.
- No separate public API: AJAX on web endpoints.
- Admin area in the same codebase, protected by `auth`.
- Global locale middleware on web stack: `ResolveLocaleFromRoute` (see `bootstrap/app.php`).

# Routing and HTTP contracts
- Public routes are locale-prefixed in `routes/web.php` with slugs from `config/routes.php`.
- Admin routes are in `routes/admin.php`, loaded by `bootstrap/app.php` inside `web` middleware.
- Admin login is separate (`/admin/login`), logout is `/logout`.

## Critical operational endpoints
- Public quote endpoint: `POST /{locale}/{availability-slug}/quote`
  - valid input: `checkin`, `checkout`
  - JSON output: `available`, `total_cents` plus technical breakdown
- Availability request endpoint: `POST /{locale}/{availability-slug}`
  - supports JSON and form submit
  - sends owner email (`BookingRequestMail`), with non-blocking fallback on mail errors
- Telegram webhook: `POST /api/telegram/webhook/{secret}` (stateless, no CSRF)
  - Receives updates from Telegram; logs `chat_id` for initial recipient setup.
  - Secret validated against `config('telegram.webhook_secret')`.
- Booking Telegram notify: `POST /admin/prenotazioni/{id}/notify-telegram` (requires `manage_bookings`)
  - Sends booking summary to all users with a non-null `telegram_chat_id`.
  - Returns JSON `{"sent": true|false}`.

# Domain invariants
- Canceled booking state is `canceled_at != null`.
- Canceled bookings do not block public availability.
- Booking restore is allowed only when no conflicts exist with active bookings or manual blocks.
- Physical booking deletion removes linked `availability_block`.
- Pricing is recurring by month/day only (no year).

# Service map
- `BookingCreationService`: creates booking + person + availability block.
- `PricingQuoteService`: single pricing engine (public quote + admin simulator).
- `InterhomePdfBookingParser`: parses Interhome PDFs into normalized records.
- `TelegramService`: sends Telegram messages via Bot API (`sendMessage`, `sendToAllRecipients`). Recipients resolved from `users.telegram_chat_id`.

# Configuration and precedence
- Source of truth booking defaults: `config/apartment.php`.
- `settings` DB only for:
  - `booking_mode`
  - `booking_external_url`
- Do not use `settings` for `min_nights`, `max_nights`, `cleaning_fee`, `linen_fee_per_person`, `hide_price_from`.
- `PricingQuoteService::calculate()` signature: `(string $checkin, string $checkout, int $guests = 1)`. Returns: `{available, nights, guests, stay_cents, cleaning_cents, linen_cents, total_cents, avg_per_night_cents}`. No discount logic.

# Quick checklist before changing backend
1. Confirm impacted endpoints/routes (`routes/web.php`, `routes/admin.php`).
2. Keep controllers thin; keep logic in services/models.
3. Verify side effects on availability, pricing, and PDF import.
4. Update impacted docs in the same change set.

# Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

## Roles
| Slug | Description |
|---|---|
| `super_admin` | Full access to all features |
| `host_owner` | Full access except `manage_users` and `import_pdf` |
| `host_keeper` | Viewer only: calendar, bookings (no `income_amount`), guests |

Roles are predefined in `RoleSeeder` — not dynamically created via UI.

## Permissions
| Slug | Protects |
|---|---|
| `view_bookings` | Lista e dettaglio prenotazioni (read-only, no `income_amount`) |
| `manage_bookings` | Crea/modifica/elimina/cancella prenotazioni |
| `import_pdf` | Importa prenotazioni da PDF Interhome |
| `view_people` | Lista e dettaglio ospiti (read-only) |
| `manage_people` | Crea/modifica/elimina ospiti |
| `view_calendar` | Visualizza calendario |
| `manage_calendar` | Crea/elimina blocchi disponibilità |
| `view_accounting` | Accesso contabilità, campo `income_amount`, widget dashboard |
| `manage_pricing` | Prezzi e sconti soggiorno |
| `manage_settings` | Impostazioni generali |
| `manage_newsletter` | Newsletter |
| `manage_users` | Gestione utenti **(non delegabile via override)** |

## How to check permissions in code
```php
// Blade
@if(auth()->user()->hasPermission('view_accounting'))

// PHP
$user->isSuperAdmin();              // true if role is super_admin
$user->hasPermission('manage_pricing'); // checks role + per-user overrides
```

Do **not** override Laravel's `can()` method. Use `hasPermission()` and `isSuperAdmin()` exclusively for admin authorization.

## How authorization is enforced
- **Route level**: `permission:<slug>` middleware on route groups in `routes/admin.php`
- **View level**: `@if(auth()->user()->hasPermission(...))` Blade conditionals
- Controllers do NOT contain authorization checks — they stay focused on business logic.

## Data model
- `users.role_id` → FK to `roles`
- `role_permissions` pivot → role's default permissions
- `user_permissions` pivot → per-user overrides (additive; `manage_users` is excluded from overrides)

## Adding a new role or permission
1. Add to `PermissionSeeder` / `RoleSeeder`
2. Add `permission:<slug>` middleware to the relevant route group in `routes/admin.php`
3. Add `@if(auth()->user()->hasPermission(...))` in affected Blade templates

# Tax Declaration (Dichiarazione dei redditi)

## Controller
`TaxDeclarationController@index` — `GET /admin/dichiarazione-redditi?year=YYYY`
- Protected by `permission:view_accounting` middleware (same group as Contabilità).
- Named route: `admin.tax-declaration.index`.

## Query logic
- Booking income: flagged with `income_tax = true`, paid (`income_paid = true`), date from `COALESCE(income_paid_at, checkout)`.
- Booking parking: flagged with `parking_tax = true`, paid (`parking_paid = true`), date from `COALESCE(parking_paid_at, checkout)`.
- Booking cleaning/linen: flagged with `cleaning_tax`/`linen_tax = true`, paid, date from `COALESCE(services_paid_at, checkout)`.
- `financial_entries`: flagged with `tax_declaration = true`, any type; `entry_date` used for year assignment.

# Financial Attachments

Polymorphic file attachments for financial movements. Documents (invoices, receipts, etc.) can be attached to either a `FinancialEntry` or a `Booking`.

## Endpoints (all under `permission:view_accounting`)
- `POST   /admin/allegati/{type}/{id}` — upload a file (`type` = `entry` | `booking`)
- `GET    /admin/allegati/{attachment}/download` — serve file download (private disk)
- `DELETE /admin/allegati/{attachment}` — delete file + DB record

## Storage
- Private disk (`local`): files saved to `storage/app/private/finance-attachments/{type}s/{id}/{uuid}.{ext}`
- Never publicly accessible; served only via authenticated controller
- Accepted: PDF, JPG, PNG, DOC, DOCX, XLS, XLSX — max 10 MB

## Model & relations
- `FinancialAttachment` model with `morphTo('attachable')`
- `FinancialEntry` and `Booking` both have `morphMany(FinancialAttachment::class, 'attachable')`
- Delete attachment → physically removes file from disk before deleting DB record

## UX
- In `finance/index`: each movement row has a 📎 icon button; count shown if > 0; clicking opens a native `<dialog>` modal with list + upload form
- In `finance/form` (edit only): attachment section rendered below the main form card
- Only flagged+paid items count toward totals (cash-basis). Flagged+unpaid items appear in the table with "Da pagare" status.

## Config defaults
`config/finance.php` key `tax_declaration_defaults`: `income`, `cleaning`, `linen` default `true`; `parking` defaults `false`.
Applied at `BookingController::store()` and via migration for existing rows.

